I walk down a narrow lane near the sea.
There is an old sweets shop here.
I go inside the shop.
There is a very good smell in the shop.
There is a man behind the counter.
I go to him.
"Hello bhaiya," I say.
"I want a box of fresh pedhas."
"This is for my office."
The shop worker smiles.
He puts Maharashtrian pedhas in a box.
He packs the box well.
"How much is this for?" I ask.
"Madam, two hundred and fifty rupees," he says.
I give him the money.
He gives me the box of sweets.
My journey is complete.
Now I need to go back home.
I am very happy today.
